e`, re-lookup of the moved key returns `slot < 0` | `assert` → `SIGABRT`. Reachable by giving `hmdel_key` a `keyoffset` inconsistent with the `keyoffset=0` used by `hmput_key` | `err29_hmdel_relookup_assert` | [x] |\n| 30 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:849`) | `b->index[i] != final_index` after re-lookup | `assert` → `SIGABRT`. Same inconsistent-`keyoffset` class; documented | `err30_hmdel_final_index_assert` | [x] |\n| 31 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:836`) | `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` **exactly** (not `>= 1`) and `string.mode == STBDS_SH_STRDUP` | frees the strdup'd key. With `mode = 2` (`STBDS_HM_PTR_TO_STRING`) the string compare still happens (`>= 1`) but the key is **not** freed — a leak the C has and the Rust must reproduce | `err31_hmdel_mode2_no_free` | [x] |\n| 32 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:854`) | `used_count < used_count_shrink_threshold && slot_count > 8` after a delete | index shrinks to `slot_count >> 1` | `err32_hmdel_shrink` | [x] |\n| 33 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:858`) | `tombstone_count > tombstone_count_threshold` (`(sc>>3)+(sc>>4)`) and shrink did not trigger | index rebuilt at the same `slot_count` | `err33_hmdel_tombstone_rebuild` | [x] |\n| 34 | `stbds_stralloc` (`lib.c:913`) | `len > a->remaining` still true after the block allocation — reachable by handing in an arena whose `storage != NULL` and whose `remaining` was set larger than the live block (`len > blocksize` path sets `remaining = 0` only when `storage == NULL`) | `assert` → `SIGABRT` | `err34_stralloc_remaining_assert` | [x] |\n| 35 | `stbds_stralloc` (`lib.c:885`) | `len <= a->remaining` (fast path) | no allocation: `p = storage->storage + remaining - len`, `remaining -= len` | `err35_stralloc_fast_path` | [x] |\n| 36 | `stbds_stralloc` (`lib.c:893-904`) | `len > blocksize` (oversize string) **and** `a->storage == NULL` | dedicated block, `sb->next = 0`, `a->storage = sb`, `a->remaining = 0`; returns `sb->storage` | `err36_stralloc_oversize_no_storage` | [x] |\n| 37 | `stbds_stralloc