{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ykjzs4phnbgivywuj57s3kt6vkftlnsbgbrifxe4aziwnocrd25q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01PkRWbk2fc71Brnk3ie6Cmf","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-T82EWy/translated_rust/ERRORS.md","old_string":"| 34 | `stbds_stralloc` (`lib.c:913`) | `len > a->remaining` still true after the block allocation — reachable by handing in an arena whose `storage != NULL` and whose `remaining` was set larger than the live block (`len > blocksize` path sets `remaining = 0` only when `storage == NULL`) | `assert` → `SIGABRT` | `err34_stralloc_remaining_assert` | [x] |","new_string":"| 34a | `stbds_stralloc` (`lib.c:913`) | `STBDS_ASSERT(len <= a->remaining)`. **Unreachable**: if `len <= remaining` on entry the `if` is skipped and the assert is trivially true; if `len > remaining` then either `len > blocksize` (the oversize branch `return`s before the assert) or `len <= blocksize` and `remaining` is set to `blocksize >= len`. Proven by exhaustive enumeration of the three paths | never fires | `err34a_stralloc_remaining_assert_unreachable` | [x] |\n| 34b | `stbds_stralloc` (`lib.c:914`) | the *reachable* failure at the same spot: an arena with `remaining > 0` but `storage == NULL` takes the fast path and dereferences `a->storage->storage` | `SIGSEGV` (NULL + 8 deref) | `err34b_stralloc_remaining_without_storage_segv` | [x] |"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5274,"cache_read_input_tokens":223146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5274,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81ea8718-705d-4eca-b08c-039f28f83148","uuid":"f1689892-bf4b-499b-ab63-b83671d6e631","timestamp":"2026-08-20T06:33:32.290Z"}
