n = INT_MIN` → `\"test_-2147483648\"` (16 chars + NUL, fits the 256-byte static) | same bytes in the static buffer, same returned pointer target contents | `err54_strkey_int_min` | [x] |\n| 55 | `stbds_hmget_key_ts` | `temp` output pointer aliasing / value on the `a == NULL` path is written **before** the return | `*temp` is `-1`; verified the callee writes through the caller's pointer | `err55_hmget_ts_temp_written` | [x] |\n| 56 | `stbds_hmfree_func` (`lib.c:575-579`) | `string.mode == STBDS_SH_STRDUP` → frees `*(char**)(a + elemsize*i)` for `i` in `1..length`. If `length <= 1` the loop is empty | double-free safety: index 0 (the default slot) is never freed | `err56_hmfree_strdup_skips_slot0` | [x] |\n| 57 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | delete the **last** element (`old_index == final_index`) | the `memmove`/re-lookup/`assert` block is skipped entirely | `err57_hmdel_last_element` | [x] |\n| 58 | `stbds_hmdel_key` | delete from a table with exactly one live entry, then delete again (key now absent) | second call: `temp = 0`, `length` unchanged | `err58_hmdel_twice` | [x] |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":43,"oldLines":8,"newStart":43,"newLines":8,"lines":[" | 26 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:821-822`) | key absent | `header->temp` stays `0` (the \"nothing deleted\" sentinel the `hmdel` macro yields), returns `a`, `length`/`used_count` unchanged | `err26_hmdel_key_absent` | [x] |"," | 27 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:828`) | `slot >= (ptrdiff_t)table->slot_count` | `assert` → `SIGABRT`. Unreachable: `stbds_hm_find_slot` masks `pos` with `slot_count-1`; documented | `err27_hmdel_slot_range_assert_unreachable` | [x] |"," | 28 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:832`) | `table->used_count >= 0` — `used_count` is `size_t`, so this is a tautology and can never fire | never aborts (also verified for the `used_count == 0` underflow case, which wraps instead of asserting) | `err28_hmdel_used_count_tautology` | [x] |","-| 29 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:846`) | after the swap-with-last `memmove`, re-lookup of the moved key returns `slot < 0` | `assert` → `SIGABRT`. Reachable by giving `hmdel_key` a `keyoffset` inconsistent with the `keyoffset=0` used by `hmput_key` | `err29_hmdel_relookup_assert` | [x] |","-| 30 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:849`) | `b->index[i] != final_index` after re-lookup | `assert` → `SIGABRT`. Same inconsistent-`keyoffset` class; documented | `err30_hmdel_final_index_assert` | [x] |","+| 29 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:846`) | after the swap-with-last `memmove`, re-lookup of the moved key returns `slot < 0`. **Reachable** with any `mode >= 2` deleting a NON-last element: the re-lookup branch tests `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` (`lib.c:842`) and so passes `&elem.key` (the *address* of the key pointer), while `stbds_hm_find_slot` tests `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING` and hashes those pointer bytes *as a string* — a different hash, so the slot is never found | `assert` → `SIGABRT` | `err29_hmdel_mode2_relookup_abort` | [x] |","+| 30 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:849`) | `b->index[i] != final_index` after a re-lookup that *did* succeed. Same `mode >= 2` class; the `slot >= 0` assert (row 29) fires first on every input we can construct, so row 30 is dominated by row 29 and never observed independently — proven by enumerating the branch | `assert` → `SIGABRT` (dominated by row 29) | `err30_hmdel_final_index_assert_dominated` | [x] |"," | 31 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:836`) | `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` **exactly** (not `>= 1`) and `string.mode == STBDS_SH_STRDUP` | frees the strdup'd key. With `mode = 2` (`STBDS_HM_PTR_TO_STRING`) the string compare still happens (`>= 1`) but the key is **not** freed — a leak the C has and the Rust must reproduce | `err31_hmdel_mode2_no_free` | [x] |"," | 32 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:854`) | `used_count < used_count_shrink_threshold && slot_count > 8` after a delete | index shrinks to `slot_count >> 1` | `err32_hmdel_shrink` | [x] |"," | 33 | `stbds_hmdel_key` (`lib.c:858`) | `tombstone_count > tombstone_count_threshold` (`(sc>>3)+(sc>>4)`) and shrink did not trigger | index rebuilt at the same `slot_count` | `err33_hmdel_tombstone_rebuild` | [x] |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
