{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sqx5hm2s7ivpovr62yrp6dgamvg6y3tzimumoiutm2t543l4q6ha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is an `stb_ds.h`-derived dynamic array + hash map (siphash-2-4, 8-slot buckets, four string-storage modes) plus the `strkey`/`arr_push` test helpers. 16 exported symbols; one public header entry (`arr_push`).\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | **0 missing.** Symbol sets are *identical in both directions* (no C-only, no Rust-only) for **both** debug and release `.so`. 0 unresolved non-libc imports. Nothing stubbed. |\n| Phase B — all `CONFIGS.md` rows | **67/67** pass across randomized inputs (fixed seeds) |\n| Phase C — all `ERRORS.md` rows | **61/61** pass, asserting the *same* sentinel/code/signal — plus 82 generic NULL / oversized-length / out-of-range-enum FFI scenarios |\n| Phase D — every feature combination | Build surface is mechanically **one** configuration: no `[features]`, no CMake `option()`, **0** `#ifdef` in the C. `scripts/check_all_features.sh` runs check + build (dev *and* release) + symbol diff + full suite. **114 tests, all green.** |\n\n## No divergence found in the translation\n\nEvery C quirk is reproduced, including ones a \"tidied-up\" port gets wrong: the asymmetric `temp_key` update between `hmput_key`'s two probe halves; `hmdel_key` testing `mode == 1` while `find_slot` tests `mode >= 1` (so **any `mode >= 2` delete of a non-last element aborts** — both do, identically); the leaked strdup key for `mode >= 2`; the signed-`int` overflow of `d[3] << 24` in the siphash tail; `512u << 55` wrapping to 0; the oversize arena splice-after-head.\n\n## Three things worth flagging\n\n1. **A harness bug I found and fixed.** Because `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` produces no rlib, **neither `cargo test` nor `cargo test --test X` rebuilds the cdylib** — every test was `dlopen`ing a stale `.so`. Proven by planting `abort()` in a hot path and watching `cargo test` pass. Fixed with `common::ensure_built` + a self-test asserting each `.so` is newer than its source.\n\n2. **Mutation testing (27 deliberate mutations, 24 caught).** The 3 misses are the same site — removing `if (hash < 2) hash += 2` — unobservable by construction (a 2⁻⁶³ siphash event), which is exactly what `ERRORS.md` row 45 documents; the invariant it protects is asserted after every one of 3 000 random ops. This also caught a genuine gap in my own tests: the `mode >= 2` strdup leak is *leak-only*, so I added an allocator-recycling detector (`err31b`).\n\n3. **One build-profile difference, asserted rather than assumed.** For inputs that drive the C into UB (store through NULL after a failed `realloc`), the **release** `.so` faults with `SIGSEGV` identically to the C; the **dev** `.so` reports \"null pointer dereference occurred\" → `SIGABRT`, because `debug_assertions` insert MIR null checks. Fatal rows therefore compare against release; all non-fatal rows compare against dev (whose overflow checks are active, so nothing silently relies on release wrapping).\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `scripts/check_all_features.sh`, and ~6 700 lines of tests. `c_src/` sources are byte-identical (only `c_src/build/` added, as the task's build instructions require); the only `Cargo.toml` change is the requested `libloading` dev-dependency."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1051,"cache_read_input_tokens":429250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1051,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81ea8718-705d-4eca-b08c-039f28f83148","uuid":"51cf1b42-0117-4f2e-a4e6-496005d75a47","timestamp":"2026-08-20T07:42:12.477Z"}
